{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WAvqmKTdQubXF5t7XAFnSd","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"MACE-MP-0 E0s isolated atom energies DFT PBE \"E0\" mace-mp foundation model\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"MolCryst-MLIPs: A Machine-Learned Interatomic Potentials Database for Molecular Crystals\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2604.13897\"},{\"title\":\"The Good, the Bad, and the Ugly of Atomistic Learning for \\\"Clusters-to-Bulk\\\" Generalization\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.16601\"},{\"title\":\"Bayesian optimization of atomic structures with prior probabilities from universal interatomic potentials\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2408.15590\"},{\"title\":\"github.com\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ACEsuit/mace\"},{\"title\":\"mace-web-interface.readthedocs.io\",\"url\":\"https://mace-web-interface.readthedocs.io/en/latest/science/models/\"},{\"title\":\"mace mp0.md\",\"url\":\"https://tricor.readthedocs.io/en/latest/_sources/algorithms/mace_mp0.md.txt\"},{\"title\":\"mace_omat_medium — Fine-tuned MACE OMAT for LiF\",\"url\":\"https://huggingface.co/jorgemunozl/mace_omat_lora_v1\"},{\"title\":\"mace mp 0\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/mace-mp-0\"},{\"title\":\"mace mp 0\",\"url\":\"https://api.emergentmind.com/topics/mace-mp-0\"},{\"title\":\"pdf.arxiv.org\",\"url\":\"https://pdf.arxiv.org/pdf/2401.00096\"}]\n\nThe search did not turn up MACE-MP-0's own official E0 table. The results give related material, and some of it conflicts.\n\n- **MolCryst-MLIPs paper (arXiv 2604.13897):** This paper lists isolated-atom reference energies for H, C, N, and O. They were computed in VASP with PBE, using a single atom in a large box and spin polarization for open-shell atoms. The values are small, about -0.003 eV for H and -1.25 eV for C. These are not the MACE-MP-0 values, and the paper does not say they are. They are a different reference setup.\n- **MACE GitHub README:** The MACE repository documents the `--E0s` option and the practice of labeling isolated atoms in the training set with `config_type=IsolatedAtom`. Its example E0s (for example, about -1029 for C and -2042 for O) are illustrative values from a training example, not documented MACE-MP-0 defaults. The same README lists MACE-MP-0 as trained on MPTrj at the PBE/PBE+U level.\n- **Clusters-to-bulk paper (arXiv 2509.16601):** This paper gives isolated-atom energies for a revPBE-D3 reference (for example, about -13.7 eV for H and -2042.9 eV for O). It is a different functional from MACE-MP-0's PBE(+U) training data.\n- **Secondary sites (mace-web-interface docs, emergentmind, tricor):** These describe MACE-MP-0 as using an energy reference based on isolated atoms and PBE(+U) data. They are not authoritative for the exact E0 values.\n\nTaken together, the sources do not confirm the specific E0 values MACE-MP-0 uses. The likely primary source is the MACE-MP-0 release or its model card, and the mace code's `E0s` handling should be checked there. The E0 magnitudes in the MolCryst table differ widely from the README example, which is a sign that reference conventions vary between studies.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5700ee4c-61b7-45c3-bc83-910d88a8b374","uuid":"34619827-ff3d-497b-b556-d649bc7e027c","timestamp":"2026-11-01T07:35:23.320Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"MACE-MP-0 E0s isolated atom energies DFT PBE \"E0\" mace-mp foundation model","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01UNCaeFxBJn42biaWsGZTfq","content":[{"title":"MolCryst-MLIPs: A Machine-Learned Interatomic Potentials Database for Molecular Crystals","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2604.13897"},{"title":"The Good, the Bad, and the Ugly of Atomistic Learning for \"Clusters-to-Bulk\" Generalization","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.16601"},{"title":"Bayesian optimization of atomic structures with prior probabilities from universal interatomic potentials","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2408.15590"},{"title":"github.com","url":"https://github.com/ACEsuit/mace"},{"title":"mace-web-interface.readthedocs.io","url":"https://mace-web-interface.readthedocs.io/en/latest/science/models/"},{"title":"mace mp0.md","url":"https://tricor.readthedocs.io/en/latest/_sources/algorithms/mace_mp0.md.txt"},{"title":"mace_omat_medium — Fine-tuned MACE OMAT for LiF","url":"https://huggingface.co/jorgemunozl/mace_omat_lora_v1"},{"title":"mace mp 0","url":"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/mace-mp-0"},{"title":"mace mp 0","url":"https://api.emergentmind.com/topics/mace-mp-0"},{"title":"pdf.arxiv.org","url":"https://pdf.arxiv.org/pdf/2401.00096"}]},"The search did not turn up MACE-MP-0's own official E0 table. The results give related material, and some of it conflicts.\n\n- **MolCryst-MLIPs paper (arXiv 2604.13897):** This paper lists isolated-atom reference energies for H, C, N, and O. They were computed in VASP with PBE, using a single atom in a large box and spin polarization for open-shell atoms. The values are small, about -0.003 eV for H and -1.25 eV for C. These are not the MACE-MP-0 values, and the paper does not say they are. They are a different reference setup.\n- **MACE GitHub README:** The MACE repository documents the `--E0s` option and the practice of labeling isolated atoms in the training set with `config_type=IsolatedAtom`. Its example E0s (for example, about -1029 for C and -2042 for O) are illustrative values from a training example, not documented MACE-MP-0 defaults. The same README lists MACE-MP-0 as trained on MPTrj at the PBE/PBE+U level.\n- **Clusters-to-bulk paper (arXiv 2509.16601):** This paper gives isolated-atom energies for a revPBE-D3 reference (for example, about -13.7 eV for H and -2042.9 eV for O). It is a different functional from MACE-MP-0's PBE(+U) training data.\n- **Secondary sites (mace-web-interface docs, emergentmind, tricor):** These describe MACE-MP-0 as using an energy reference based on isolated atoms and PBE(+U) data. They are not authoritative for the exact E0 values.\n\nTaken together, the sources do not confirm the specific E0 values MACE-MP-0 uses. The likely primary source is the MACE-MP-0 release or its model card, and the mace code's `E0s` handling should be checked there. The E0 magnitudes in the MolCryst table differ widely from the README example, which is a sign that reference conventions vary between studies."],"durationSeconds":6.797689117000002,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01WAvqmKTdQubXF5t7XAFnSd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019MTwDeVQLLBLETZt6C2FPE","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"atomic oxygen binding energy Cu(111) fcc site DFT eV relative to gas-phase O atom\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Quantum Many-Body Simulations of Catalytic Metal Surfaces\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2508.13036\"},{\"title\":\"InterPhon: Ab initio Interface Phonon Calculations within a 3D Electronic Structure Framework\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2012.04198\"},{\"title\":\"arxiv.org\",\"url\":\"https://www.arxiv.org/pdf/2505.12914\"},{\"title\":\"Structural and electronic properties of atomic oxygen adsorption on Cu(111) surface: A first-principles investigation\",\"url\":\"https://bvbvf1.bib-bvb.de/vufind/PrimoRecord/cdi_chongqing_primary_44769476\"},{\"title\":\"s11433 012 4868 5\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/s11433-012-4868-5.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"First principles study of oxidation resistance of atomically flat Cu(111) surface\",\"url\":\"https://archive.aps.org/mar/2022/g47/5\"},{\"title\":\"First principles study of oxidation resistance of atomically flat Cu(111) surface\",\"url\":\"https://https-meetings--archive-aps-org-443.webvpn1.xju.edu.cn/mar/2022/g47/5/\"},{\"title\":\"PhysRevB 73 165424\",\"url\":\"https://condensed.physics.usyd.edu.au/old_website/papers_aloy/PhysRevB_73_165424.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"P 46 a11 6122919\",\"url\":\"https://accms.mobility.niche.tohoku.ac.jp/ACCMS-11/POSTER/P-46_a11_6122919.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"4.7 Article\",\"url\":\"https://www.peeref.com/works/757048\"}]\n\nThe search turned up several DFT values for O on the Cu(111) fcc hollow, but they are not directly comparable because the papers use different sign conventions and settings.\n\n- **Closest match to your query:** One study reports an fcc binding energy of -5.000 eV and an hcp value of -4.905 eV. It defines binding energy as the slab energy minus the bare slab and the gas-phase O atom reference, so negative values mean favorable binding. Its formula subtracts the bare copper surface energy and the isolated gas-phase oxygen atom energy from the adsorbed configuration energy, normalized per adsorbed O atom. The fcc site is listed at -5.000 eV and the hcp site at -4.905 eV.\n- **Different magnitude, same site preference:** A separate Tohoku poster reports -6.37 eV for fcc and -6.26 eV for hcp, and finds that the fcc hollow is the most favorable site. Its exact reference convention is not stated in the snippet, so the offset from the -5.0 eV value is not explained by the sources here. The calculated adsorption energies were -6.37 eV and -6.26 eV for the fcc and hcp hollow sites, respectively.\n- **Opposite sign convention:** A 2008-era PRB paper defines binding energy so that positive values indicate stability relative to a free oxygen atom. A positive number indicates that the adsorption is exothermic and stable with respect to the free oxygen atom.\n- **fcc vs. hcp gap:** A third study (InterPhon, 0.25 ML coverage) reports the fcc site as about 0.13 eV more strongly bound than hcp, which is consistent with the -5.000 vs -4.905 eV difference of roughly 0.10 eV. While the electronic energy of O-FCC(2×2) is lower than that of O-HCP(2×2) by 0.13 eV, the vibrational energy is higher in the FCC site.\n\nBottom line: the fcc hollow is consistently the preferred site in these DFT studies, with fcc-hcp differences of about 0.1 eV. The absolute values (about -5 eV vs. about -6.4 eV) depend on the reference state and setup, so check the sign convention and the gas-phase O reference before comparing numbers across papers.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5700ee4c-61b7-45c3-bc83-910d88a8b374","uuid":"54676096-fc65-4d79-a1ce-e7c706902024","timestamp":"2026-11-01T07:35:23.921Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"atomic oxygen binding energy Cu(111) fcc