{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgbpjJiUTvwSqNprb5z9C","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016Bgdg3azUaY4b8S4AL4d3S","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /work; cat > /work/scripts/result.json <<'E'\n{\"candidate\": \"O on Cu(111)\", \"family\": \"metal surface adsorbate\", \"tier\": \"trust\",\n \"property\": \"adsorption_energy\", \"value\": -4.84, \"units\": \"eV\", \"uncertainty\": 0.3,\n \"method\": {\"engine\": \"ALCHEMI env / ASE 3.29 + mace-torch 0.3.15 (GPU, float64)\", \"model\": \"MACE-MPA-0 medium (macempa0mediummodel)\",\n   \"protocol\": \"0 K static relaxation (BFGS, fmax 0.01 eV/A); E_ads = E(slab+O) - E(slab) - E(O atom, isolated, 20 A box); fcc/hcp/top/bridge starting sites; bottom half of slab fixed\",\n   \"ensemble\": null, \"timestep_fs\": null, \"n_atoms\": 37, \"sim_length_ps\": null,\n   \"slab\": \"Cu(111) p(3x3), 4 layers, 10 A vacuum each side, 1/9 ML O; convergence checks p(2x2)/p(4x4) 4 layers and p(3x3) 5 layers\",\n   \"site\": \"fcc hollow\", \"lattice_constant_A\": 3.640},\n \"flags\": [],\n \"note\": \"Most stable site = fcc hollow: fcc -4.837, hcp -4.783, top -3.082 eV (p3x3, 4 layers); a bridge start relaxes into fcc, so bridge is not a minimum. Cu-O = 1.90 A. Convergence: p(4x4) -4.845, p(3x3) 5 layers -4.838, p(2x2) (1/4 ML) -4.904 eV, so numerical error is about 0.01 eV at <=1/9 ML. Same slabs referenced to 1/2 O2 (MACE): -1.69 eV. PREMISE: a well-defined 0 K electronic adsorption energy (no ZPE). The isolated-O energy is never predicted by the network; it equals the model's E0 (-1.548 eV). This is meaningful only because MACE foundation-model E0s are spin-polarized PBE isolated-atom energies. That is consistent with an independent VASP-PBE spin-polarized O atom (-1.531 eV, arXiv 2604.13897). VALIDATION (same setup): bulk Cu a0 3.640 A vs experiment ~3.615 A (+0.7%, typical PBE); Cu cohesive energy 3.50 eV vs experiment ~3.49 eV (this exercises the isolated-atom reference path); O2 De 6.29 eV vs experiment ~5.2 eV. The model reproduces the known PBE O2 overbinding of ~1 eV. Literature DFT anchor: one PBE-type study found by web search reports fcc -5.00 / hcp -4.91 eV vs O atom (Sci China Phys Mech Astron, doi 10.1007/s11433-012-4868-5, not independently re-read), 0.16 eV more binding than this result; fcc preference agrees. UNCERTAINTY +/-0.3 eV covers MLIP-vs-PBE error for an out-of-training-distribution surface+adsorbate (MPtrj/sAlex are mostly bulk), spread between DFT setups, and slab convergence. It does NOT cover the error of PBE itself vs the true (experimental) value. For an atom-referenced O binding energy that error may be several tenths of an eV (overbinding), as the O2 test shows. No direct experimental value referenced to the O atom was used.\"}\nE\n./board post property_result @/work/scripts/result.json --parent cd358502-e41f-4db3-9894-59ccf874baea"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":418,"cache_read_input_tokens":42097,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":418,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5700ee4c-61b7-45c3-bc83-910d88a8b374","uuid":"cde9693c-47bd-435b-9384-22164769c48a","timestamp":"2026-11-01T07:36:12.615Z","request_id":"req_011CgbpjJL9mKzCDQFNHtwee","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_016Bgdg3azUaY4b8S4AL4d3S":{"command":"cd /work; cat > /work/scripts/result.json <<'E'\n{\"candidate\": \"O on Cu(111)\", \"family\": \"metal surface adsorbate\", \"tier\": \"trust\",\n \"property\": \"adsorption_energy\", \"value\": -4.84, \"units\": \"eV\", \"uncertainty\": 0.3,\n \"method\": {\"engine\": \"ALCHEMI env / ASE 3.29 + mace-torch 0.3.15 (GPU, float64)\", \"model\": \"MACE-